        "sample_brief": {
          "markdown": "# 5-Part Research Brief: Greedy Conditional Transfer Entropy Under Non-Stationary Regime Shifts\n\n**Anchored Classic:** 1. Schreiber (2000) - Transfer Entropy (Module 02)\n\n## 1. Gap Analysis (Derived from Q7 Limitation)\nBivariate TE fails under hidden confounders, and static conditional TE assumes time-invariant transition densities.\n\n## 2. Falsifiable Hypothesis (Q8 Extension)\nWindowed adaptive KSG Conditional TE combined with BH-FDR (T >= T_80) suppresses confounder false positives across regime shifts.\n\n## 3. Minimal Model Architecture\n3-tier sliding-window KSG estimator with circular time-shift surrogates and Benjamini-Hochberg step-up thresholding.\n\n## 4. Null Baseline & Sensitivity Validation Plan\nTrack A Monte Carlo calibration solving T_80 for 80% power alongside Track B shuffled-phase null model comparison (Cohen's d > 1.5).\n\n## 5. Expected Defensible Claim\nConditioned multi-lag inference eliminates >90% of indirect cascade/common-driver artifacts while controlling FDP <= 0.05.\n",
          "json": "{\n  \"title\": \"Greedy Conditional Transfer Entropy Under Non-Stationary Regime Shifts\",\n  \"anchored_paper\": \"1. Schreiber (2000) - Transfer Entropy\",\n  \"gap_analysis\": \"Bivariate TE fails under hidden confounders, and static conditional TE assumes time-invariant transition densities.\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Windowed adaptive KSG Conditional TE combined with BH-FDR (T >= T_80) suppresses confounder false positives across regime shifts.\",\n  \"model_architecture\": \"3-tier sliding-window KSG estimator with circular time-shift surrogates and Benjamini-Hochberg step-up thresholding.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Track A Monte Carlo calibration solving T_80 for 80% power alongside Track B shuffled-phase null model comparison (Cohen's d > 1.5).\",\n  \"expected_claim\": \"Conditioned multi-lag inference eliminates >90% of indirect cascade/common-driver artifacts while controlling FDP <= 0.05.\"\n}"
        }
