          "markdown": "# 5-Part Research Brief: Grand Synthesis: Decentralized Computation & Statistical Falsifiability Across Complex Systems\n\n**Anchored Classic:** 5. Tero et al. (2010) - Physarum Tokyo Rail (Module 06)\n\n## 1. Gap Analysis (Derived from Q7 Limitation)\nObservational metrics fail under confounders while generative ABMs lack standardized null baselines and power guarantees.\n\n## 2. Falsifiable Hypothesis (Q8 Extension)\nPairing Conditional TE + BH-FDR (T >= T_80) with distribution-preserving null models cleanly separates genuine emergence from noise.\n\n## 3. Minimal Model Architecture\nUnified 8-module toolkit linking PID/TE inference, ECA/GA computation, RBN/Physarum/Vicsek networks, and strategic market dynamics.\n\n## 4. Null Baseline & Sensitivity Validation Plan\nExecute Track A BH-FDR power calibration (target 80%) and Track B Cohen's d > 1.5 across all workshop architectures.\n\n## 5. Expected Defensible Claim\nVerified reproducible separations across all 4 complex-systems pillars with controlled false discovery below 5%.\n",
